  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/000I">Lemma <span data-tag="000I">3.9.1</span>.</a> For every cardinal $\kappa $, there exists a set $A$ such that every element of $A$ is a scheme and such that for every scheme $S$ with $\text{size}(S) \leq \kappa $, there is an element $X \in A$ such that $X \cong S$ (isomorphism of schemes). </p>
